"""Topic development follows the supplied branches, then distinct follow-up questions."""
from exam_common import case, p, q, section, coverage as c
G='speaking-part3'

def make(slug,title,focus,prompt,ideas,paragraphs,questions,vocabulary,source='practice',page=None):
    requirements=['Phát triển luận điểm và ba nhánh gợi ý; có thể thêm ý riêng phù hợp.', 'Mỗi ý cần giải thích hoặc ví dụ, không chỉ đọc tên nhánh.', 'Sau bài nói chính, trả lời riêng ba câu hỏi mở rộng.']
    return case(G,slug,title,focus,'development','Phát triển chủ đề',prompt,requirements,paragraphs,vocabulary,
        source=source,page=page,ideas=ideas,sections=[section('Câu hỏi mở rộng',questions)],
        checks=[c('Nhánh '+str(i)+': '+idea,paragraphs[i]['text']) for i,idea in enumerate(ideas,1)])

def samples():
    return [
make('travel-benefits','Lợi ích của việc đi du lịch','Refreshment, the economy and knowledge',
    'Explain the benefits of travelling. Develop the suggested ideas below, adding your own points if useful.',
    ['Feeling refreshed','Supporting the economy','Learning more about the world'],[
        p('Mở chủ đề','I would like to talk about the benefits of travelling. A trip can do more than give us photographs to share. It can provide a break from daily routines, support businesses in the destination and help us understand places beyond our own neighbourhood.', 'Dẫn đúng ba nhánh của sơ đồ nguồn.'),
        p('Thư giãn','First, travelling can help people feel refreshed. Spending a few days in a different setting gives us something new to focus on instead of the same work and household tasks. For example, a quiet weekend by the sea might give a busy office worker time to rest and return with more energy.', 'Ví dụ giả định bằng might, không hứa chữa bệnh.'),
        p('Kinh tế','Travelling also supports the economy of the places we visit. Visitors pay for rooms, meals, transport and local activities. If they choose a small family restaurant or a local guide, some of that spending reaches people who live in the area. This can create work beyond the larger hotels.', 'Đổi góc từ du khách sang cộng đồng ở nhánh kinh tế.'),
        p('Kiến thức','Finally, travel can improve our knowledge. Visiting a historical building or talking to a local resident can make a place more meaningful than a short description in a book. We may learn about unfamiliar food, customs or ways of working, and notice that our own habits are not the only possible ones.', 'Đúng nhánh mở mang kiến thức.'),
        p('Kết','To sum up, travel can refresh us, support local livelihoods and broaden our understanding. These benefits are more likely when we allow time to explore respectfully rather than rushing through a list of attractions.', 'Tổng hợp không đổi thành tác hại du lịch.')],
    [q('Which time of year suits your trips?', 'Personally, I prefer travelling in spring because the weather is often comfortable for walking. I still check the conditions at the destination, as a pleasant season in one place may be very different elsewhere.'),
     q('Name a country you hope to visit and explain why.', 'I would like to visit Japan because I am interested in its traditional gardens and everyday food. I would spend time in a smaller town as well as a large city to see different sides of the country.'),
     q('Would you choose a domestic or an overseas holiday?', 'For a short holiday, I would choose somewhere in my own country. Travelling is usually easier to arrange, and I can spend more time at the destination. For a longer break, going abroad would be exciting.')],
    [('daily routines','sinh hoạt thường ngày'),('local livelihoods','sinh kế địa phương'),('broaden our understanding','mở rộng hiểu biết')],source='dthu',page=17),
make('teen-reading','Khuyến khích thanh thiếu niên đọc sách','Knowledge, relaxation and memory',
    'Make the case for encouraging teenagers to read. Use the three suggested benefits or develop other relevant ideas.',
    ['Building knowledge','Relaxing','Exercising memory'],[
        p('Mở chủ đề','I support encouraging teenagers to read regularly. Reading offers a quiet activity that they can choose for themselves, and it can help with knowledge, relaxation and remembering information. The aim should be to build an enjoyable habit, not to turn every book into another school test.', 'Luận điểm đúng đề; không dùng khung khó khăn–giải pháp.'),
        p('Kiến thức','First, books can introduce teenagers to subjects beyond their daily experience. A story set in another country may lead a reader to learn about a different way of life, while a simple science book can explain how ordinary things work. Reading also exposes learners to words used in meaningful situations.', 'Nêu cách hình thành kiến thức, không chỉ nói good.'),
        p('Thư giãn','Another benefit is relaxation. Following an interesting story can give a teenager a break from messages, homework and social pressure. For example, reading a few pages before bed may provide a calmer end to the day than moving rapidly between short online videos. The book needs to match the reader’s interests for this to be enjoyable.', 'Lợi ích có điều kiện lựa chọn sách.'),
        p('Ghi nhớ','Reading also gives people practice in remembering details. To understand a story, we keep track of characters, earlier events and the connections between them. Recalling why a character made a decision encourages active attention. This does not mean every book automatically improves every kind of memory, but it does create opportunities to practise remembering and connecting information.', 'Diễn đạt vừa mức; tránh khẳng định sức khỏe nhận thức quá mức.'),
        p('Kết','In conclusion, reading can expand knowledge, offer a relaxing break and encourage active recall. Giving teenagers a choice of accessible books is a useful way to help those benefits become part of everyday life.', 'Khớp cả ba nhánh.')],
    [q('How might reading choices differ between generations?', 'My parents often choose newspapers and books about practical skills, while I read more short fiction and technology articles. However, interests vary within every generation, so I would not assume that all older people enjoy the same material.'),
     q('Should public money provide free access to books?', 'I think public libraries are a sensible way to provide free access. People can share a wide range of books without everyone needing a personal copy. The collection should reflect local needs and include accessible digital options where useful.'),
     q('How can parents encourage children to enjoy books?', 'Parents can read together with children and let them choose some of the books. Asking what they liked about a story may help more than testing every detail. Seeing adults read for pleasure can also make the habit feel normal.')],
    [('social pressure','áp lực xã hội'),('keep track of','theo dõi và ghi nhớ'),('read for pleasure','đọc để thưởng thức')],source='ufls',page=16),
make('public-parks','Công viên công cộng cần được gìn giữ','Exercise, social contact and green space',
    'Public parks are important for city residents. Develop this statement using the ideas below and any relevant examples.',
    ['Places for physical activity','Opportunities to meet people','Access to green surroundings'],[
        p('Mở','In my opinion, public parks are an important part of a city because they offer shared space outside homes and workplaces. Their value is not limited to how attractive they look. They can support physical activity, give neighbours opportunities to meet and make green surroundings available to people who have no garden.', 'Nêu luận điểm và ba góc triển khai.'),
        p('Vận động','First, a park gives residents somewhere to walk, run or play without paying for a private sports club. An older person might take a gentle walk in the morning, while children can play after school. Clear paths and suitable seating make the space useful to people with different needs.', 'Ví dụ hai nhóm, không gán một hoạt động cho mọi người.'),
        p('Gặp gỡ','Parks also create opportunities for social contact. People who regularly use the same walking route may begin to recognise one another and have short conversations. A family picnic or a small community activity can bring neighbours together. This is especially valuable in areas where residents spend most of their time inside separate flats.', 'Giải thích quá trình quen nhau từ gặp lặp lại.'),
        p('Không gian xanh','Finally, green surroundings provide a change from busy roads and buildings. Trees can offer shade, and a quiet corner gives residents somewhere to sit and read. For someone living in a small flat, access to this space may make a substantial difference to the experience of daily city life.', 'Lợi ích gần gũi, không dùng số liệu không nguồn.'),
        p('Kết','To sum up, parks support movement, social connections and access to greenery. Cities should maintain them carefully and keep them welcoming so that these benefits are available to a wide range of residents.', 'Khép đúng luận điểm.')],
    [q('What makes a park attractive to different age groups?', 'Different users need different things. Children may want play areas, while older residents may value shade and benches. Clear paths and clean toilets help almost everyone, so I would start with those basic facilities.'),
     q('Should visitors pay to enter ordinary city parks?', 'I would generally keep ordinary parks free because they are shared spaces used frequently by local residents. Charging every visit might discourage families with limited money. Special events could have separate fees if necessary.'),
     q('How can residents help care for a park?', 'They can use bins, avoid damaging plants and report broken equipment. A neighbourhood clean-up can help, but regular maintenance should still be organised properly rather than depend entirely on volunteers.')],
    [('physical activity','hoạt động thể chất'),('social contact','giao tiếp xã hội'),('green surroundings','môi trường cây xanh')]),
make('learning-language','Học ngoại ngữ mở ra cơ hội','Communication, work and cultural understanding',
    'Learning another language can create valuable opportunities. Explain this view with the suggested ideas and examples.',
    ['Communicating with more people','Opportunities at work','Understanding other cultures'],[
        p('Mở','I would like to talk about the opportunities that come from learning another language. Even basic skills can make some everyday situations easier, and stronger skills can open further possibilities. Three useful benefits are communicating with more people, taking part in different kinds of work and understanding cultures more directly.', 'Không hứa học ngoại ngữ tự động có lương cao.'),
        p('Giao tiếp','First, another language allows us to speak to people we might otherwise struggle to understand. A traveller can ask for directions, explain a simple problem or have a short conversation with a host. These exchanges can make a visit more independent and personal than relying on someone else for every message.', 'Một ví dụ đời thường dễ tự diễn đạt.'),
        p('Công việc','Language skills may also expand opportunities at work. A receptionist who can answer visitors’ questions clearly can take on tasks involving international guests. Someone in a technical job may gain access to instructions or training material in another language. The language supports the work, although professional knowledge is still necessary.', 'Gắn ngoại ngữ với năng lực chuyên môn, không thay thế.'),
        p('Văn hóa','Finally, language gives us a closer connection to another culture. Songs, stories and ordinary conversations can reveal humour and habits that are difficult to translate fully. For example, learning how people make polite requests can teach us something about social relationships as well as vocabulary and grammar.', 'Có cơ chế hiểu văn hóa qua ngôn ngữ.'),
        p('Kết','In conclusion, learning another language is useful for communication, work and cultural understanding. Progress may be gradual, but using a small amount regularly can turn knowledge from a textbook into a practical skill.', 'Kết gọn, nhất quán.')],
    [q('Should children begin another language early?', 'Early exposure can be useful if it is enjoyable and appropriate for their age. Songs and games may work better than heavy grammar exercises. The quality and consistency of teaching matter as well as the starting age.'),
     q('Can translation tools replace language learning?', 'They can help with quick messages and unfamiliar words, but I would not rely on them for every conversation. Knowing some of the language helps us notice mistakes and respond naturally when the situation changes.'),
     q('What keeps adults motivated to learn?', 'A clear personal use can help. An adult might practise booking a room before a trip or answering questions at work. Small tasks with visible progress can feel more motivating than studying a long list without using it.')],
    [('professional knowledge','kiến thức chuyên môn'),('polite requests','lời đề nghị lịch sự'),('gradual progress','tiến bộ từng bước')]),
make('volunteering','Sinh viên nên tham gia tình nguyện','Practical skills, community help and connections',
    'Volunteering can be valuable for university students. Develop the topic using the following ideas.',
    ['Developing practical skills','Helping the community','Building connections'],[
        p('Mở','In my view, volunteering can be a valuable part of university life when students choose realistic commitments. It gives them a way to use their time for something beyond classes. The main benefits include developing practical skills, helping meet community needs and building relationships with people they might not otherwise meet.', 'Có điều kiện về mức cam kết, không bắt buộc mọi người làm nhiều giờ.'),
        p('Kỹ năng','First, voluntary work can develop skills that are difficult to learn only from lectures. A student helping organise a book donation needs to communicate with donors, keep records and plan transport. If arrangements change, the student has to solve practical problems with others instead of simply describing teamwork in an assignment.', 'Ví dụ nhiệm vụ cụ thể cho kỹ năng cụ thể.'),
        p('Cộng đồng','Second, students can make a useful contribution when their work responds to a real request. For example, helping children practise reading each week can provide steady support to a local club. Listening to the organisation matters: volunteers should learn what is needed rather than arrive with a project that creates extra work for the people they hope to help.', 'Đặt nhu cầu người được hỗ trợ làm trung tâm.'),
        p('Kết nối','Volunteering also brings students into contact with different age groups and backgrounds. Working beside experienced organisers can help them understand local issues and develop friendships. These connections may continue after an event and encourage students to feel that they belong to the community around their university.', 'Không chỉ coi tình nguyện là làm đẹp CV.'),
        p('Kết','To sum up, volunteering can build skills, support others and strengthen social connections. A small regular commitment that a student can keep is often more useful than promising many hours and then failing to attend.', 'Kết với cách tham gia bền vững.')],
    [q('Should volunteering be compulsory for students?', 'I would offer opportunities rather than require identical hours from everyone. Some students already work or care for family members. Encouragement and flexible options are more likely to support meaningful participation.'),
     q('How can a student choose a suitable project?', 'The student should consider their available time, skills and interests, then ask the organisation what help is needed. A short introductory session can show whether the role is a realistic fit before a longer commitment.'),
     q('What problems can poorly organised volunteering create?', 'Volunteers may arrive without training or leave tasks unfinished. The organisation then has to spend extra time correcting work. Clear responsibilities, supervision and honest discussion of availability can reduce those problems.')],
    [('practical skills','kỹ năng thực tế'),('steady support','sự hỗ trợ đều đặn'),('a regular commitment','cam kết tham gia đều')]),
make('family-meals','Bữa ăn chung có ý nghĩa với gia đình','Conversation, routines and shared responsibilities',
    'Sharing meals can strengthen family life. Explain this statement using the suggested ideas.',
    ['Time to communicate','A shared daily routine','Sharing household responsibilities'],[
        p('Mở','I believe sharing meals can strengthen family life, even if everyone cannot sit together every day. A meal creates a natural reason to pause and spend time in the same place. It can support conversation, give the family a shared routine and provide opportunities to divide everyday responsibilities.', 'Không mặc định mọi gia đình có cùng lịch.'),
        p('Giao tiếp','First, a shared meal gives family members a chance to hear about one another’s day. A child might mention something that happened at school, or a parent might explain a change in work plans. These small exchanges can prevent people from knowing very little about the lives of those they live with.', 'Giải thích bằng chuyện hằng ngày, không lời khuyên tâm lý chuyên sâu.'),
        p('Thói quen','Second, regular meals together can make a busy week feel more predictable. For example, a family might keep Sunday lunch free even when weekday schedules are different. Having one reliable time to meet means conversations do not depend entirely on everyone happening to be available at once.', 'Có lựa chọn thực tế thay cho yêu cầu ngày nào cũng đủ người.'),
        p('Chia việc','Preparing and clearing up after meals also offers a way to share responsibility. One person can cook while another lays the table and someone else washes the dishes. Children can take on suitable small tasks. This makes the meal a joint activity and helps prevent all the work from falling on one family member.', 'Liên hệ công bằng trong công việc nhà.'),
        p('Kết','In conclusion, shared meals can support communication, a sense of routine and cooperation at home. The important point is making the time welcoming, not insisting on a perfect dinner or turning every conversation into a criticism.', 'Chốt ý xây dựng và gần gũi.')],
    [q('Why do some families find it hard to eat together?', 'Work shifts, school activities and long journeys can make schedules difficult to match. It does not always mean people are unwilling. Choosing one realistic meal each week may be a useful starting point.'),
     q('Should phones be put away during meals?', 'Personally, I would prefer that for an ordinary family meal because messages can interrupt conversation. There may be exceptions, such as an urgent work call, but the expectation should be discussed together.'),
     q('Can eating out serve the same purpose?', 'Yes, eating out can still give a family time to talk. However, it may cost more and does not involve sharing the preparation. I think it can complement home meals rather than replace them completely.')],
    [('shared routine','thói quen sinh hoạt chung'),('lays the table','dọn bàn ăn'),('joint activity','hoạt động làm cùng nhau')]),
make('public-transport','Giao thông công cộng tốt hơn giúp thành phố','Road space, access and travel costs',
    'Improving public transport can benefit a city. Develop this view using the three suggested ideas.',
    ['Using road space more efficiently','Access for people without private vehicles','More affordable daily travel'],[
        p('Mở','In my opinion, better public transport can improve daily life in a city. The benefit depends on services being reliable and connected to the places people need to reach. When those conditions are met, public transport can use road space efficiently, improve access and reduce the cost of regular journeys.', 'Điều kiện để tác dụng xảy ra, tránh hứa cứ có xe buýt là hết tắc.'),
        p('Không gian đường','First, a bus can carry many passengers in less road space than the same number of people travelling separately in cars. If services are frequent and convenient, some drivers may choose them instead. Priority lanes and sensible routes can help keep buses moving, making the alternative more attractive during busy periods.', 'Có cơ chế và điều kiện thay đổi hành vi.'),
        p('Khả năng tiếp cận','Second, public transport gives options to residents who cannot drive or do not own a vehicle. A student may need to reach college, while an older person may want to visit family. Clear information, suitable stops and accessible vehicles help these passengers make journeys without depending on a lift from someone else.', 'Chỉ rõ các nhóm và nhu cầu.'),
        p('Chi phí','Finally, dependable services can make daily travel more affordable. A regular passenger may be able to use a season ticket instead of paying for fuel, parking and vehicle maintenance. This is particularly useful when money is limited. However, fares still need to be considered alongside the number of changes and the time required for the journey.', 'Tính cả tiền và thời gian, không giả định phương án luôn rẻ hơn.'),
        p('Kết','To sum up, good public transport supports efficient road use, wider access and affordable travel. Improving reliability and convenience is essential if these potential benefits are to become part of residents’ normal routines.', 'Tổng hợp đúng ba nhánh.')],
    [q('What would encourage more drivers to take the bus?', 'Reliable arrival times and routes that match actual journeys would help. People also need clear information and reasonable comfort. A low fare alone may not persuade someone if the service regularly makes them late.'),
     q('Should public transport be free?', 'Free travel could help some passengers, but services still need money to operate. I would first consider reliable service and targeted discounts for those who need them most, then assess whether a wider free scheme is affordable.'),
     q('How can small towns improve transport?', 'They may not need the same system as a large city. A smaller number of routes connecting schools, markets and health services could be useful. Timetables should reflect when residents actually need to travel.')],
    [('road space','diện tích mặt đường'),('season ticket','vé tháng hoặc vé dài hạn'),('vehicle maintenance','bảo dưỡng phương tiện')]),
make('practical-school','Trường học nên dạy kỹ năng sống thực tế','Money, household tasks and everyday decisions',
    'Schools should help students develop practical life skills. Explain this view with the ideas below.',
    ['Managing money','Handling basic household tasks','Making everyday decisions'],[
        p('Mở','I support the idea that schools should help students develop practical life skills alongside academic knowledge. Young people eventually need to manage ordinary responsibilities for themselves. Lessons about money, household tasks and everyday decisions can make that transition less confusing, especially when students have few chances to practise these things elsewhere.', 'Nêu alongside, không thay toàn bộ môn học bằng kỹ năng sống.'),
        p('Tiền bạc','First, students can learn simple ways to manage money. Planning a small budget helps them see the difference between essential costs and optional purchases. For example, a class activity could ask students to divide a limited weekly allowance between transport, food and savings. The purpose is understanding choices, not teaching everyone to follow an identical spending pattern.', 'Ví dụ mô phỏng, không tư vấn đầu tư.'),
        p('Việc nhà','Basic household skills are useful when students move away from home. Knowing how to prepare a simple meal, read a washing label or keep a shared kitchen clean can prevent avoidable difficulties. These tasks also show that looking after a home involves work that should be shared fairly rather than left automatically to one person.', 'Kỹ năng cụ thể, không khuôn mẫu giới.'),
        p('Ra quyết định','Practical lessons can also develop decision-making. Students might compare phone plans by looking at total cost and what they actually need, instead of choosing the most attractive advertisement. Explaining their choice encourages them to ask questions and consider consequences. That habit can transfer to many ordinary decisions outside school.', 'Cơ chế chuyển từ bài học sang đời sống.'),
        p('Kết','In conclusion, practical skills can help students handle money, contribute at home and make thoughtful choices. Schools can include short applied activities within existing subjects, so these lessons support academic learning rather than compete with it unnecessarily.', 'Đưa cách tích hợp ngắn gọn.')],
    [q('Should parents or schools teach these skills?', 'Both can contribute. Parents can offer daily practice, while schools can provide a common starting point for students with different home experiences. Cooperation is more useful than assuming one side should do everything.'),
     q('How could practical skills be assessed?', 'Students could complete a realistic task and explain their choices. For example, they might prepare a simple budget for a class trip. Assessment should value the reasoning and safe process, not only a polished final result.'),
     q('Would these lessons reduce time for academic subjects?', 'They could if introduced without planning. However, some activities fit existing subjects: budgeting can practise mathematics, and comparing advertisements can support reading. Careful integration would reduce unnecessary competition for lesson time.')],
    [('weekly allowance','tiền được cho hằng tuần'),('essential costs','chi phí thiết yếu'),('consider consequences','cân nhắc hệ quả')]),
make('flexible-work','Lịch làm việc linh hoạt có ích thế nào?','Personal schedules, commuting and concentration',
    'Flexible working arrangements can benefit employees. Develop the suggested ideas, explaining when the benefits are realistic.',
    ['Managing personal responsibilities','Reducing commuting pressure','Choosing productive working periods'],[
        p('Mở','Flexible working arrangements can benefit employees when the job allows them and expectations are clear. Flexibility may involve different starting times or some work from home, rather than simply working fewer hours. It can help people manage personal responsibilities, reduce commuting pressure and organise tasks around periods when they can concentrate well.', 'Định nghĩa đúng phạm vi linh hoạt.'),
        p('Trách nhiệm cá nhân','First, adjustable hours can make it easier to manage responsibilities outside work. A parent might start earlier so that they can collect a child from school, while still completing the agreed hours. This can reduce repeated conflicts between work and home. The arrangement needs to be agreed with the employer so that colleagues know when the person is available.', 'Không biến linh hoạt thành tự ý vắng mặt.'),
        p('Đi lại','Second, changing travel times can reduce the pressure of commuting at the busiest point of the day. Someone who starts later may avoid the worst traffic, and working from home occasionally removes that journey altogether. The saved time can be used for rest or personal tasks rather than spent waiting on a crowded road.', 'Cơ chế tiết kiệm thời gian, không số liệu bịa.'),
        p('Tập trung','Finally, some tasks are easier to complete during a quiet period. An employee preparing a detailed report may work best early in the morning before meetings begin. Flexibility can help protect that time. However, team discussions and customer service still require coordination, so individual preferences cannot be the only consideration.', 'Thừa nhận công việc cần phối hợp.'),
        p('Kết','To sum up, flexible arrangements can support everyday responsibilities, easier travel and focused work. Their value depends on clear communication and the type of job, rather than a rule that everyone should work in exactly the same way.', 'Kết có phạm vi, không áp dụng mọi nghề.')],
    [q('Can every job offer the same flexibility?', 'No. A nurse or shop assistant needs to be present at particular times, while some office tasks can be done remotely. Flexibility should be designed around the service being provided, perhaps through shift choices where remote work is impossible.'),
     q('What difficulties can working from home create?', 'Some people have limited space or find it hard to stop working at the end of the day. Regular contact with colleagues and a clear finishing time can help, but home conditions differ from person to person.'),
     q('How should managers judge work under flexible arrangements?', 'They should agree on useful outcomes and realistic deadlines, while keeping communication clear. Time spent visibly online is not always a good measure. Some tasks still require scheduled availability, so expectations should reflect the role.')],
    [('adjustable hours','giờ làm có thể điều chỉnh'),('commuting pressure','áp lực đi lại hằng ngày'),('focused work','công việc cần tập trung')]),
make('local-shopping','Mua hàng tại địa phương có lợi gì?','Local jobs, personal service and neighbourhood life',
    'Local shops can make a valuable contribution to a neighbourhood. Develop the topic using these ideas.',
    ['Supporting local employment','Providing personal service','Keeping neighbourhoods active'],[
        p('Mở','I would like to talk about the value of local shops. Online shopping and large supermarkets are convenient, but small shops can still contribute something important to a neighbourhood. They can support local employment, offer personal service and give residents reasons to spend time in the streets around their homes.', 'Luận điểm không phủ nhận các hình thức mua sắm khác.'),
        p('Việc làm','First, local shops create work for owners and staff, and some buy supplies from nearby businesses. A small bakery, for instance, might employ local assistants and use a nearby delivery service. When customers choose to shop there regularly, they help maintain those jobs. This does not mean every product is locally made, so the benefit depends on the business.', 'Giới hạn tránh suy diễn mọi đồng tiền đều ở lại địa phương.'),
        p('Dịch vụ','Second, a small shop may be able to give personal attention. An owner who knows regular customers can remember their preferences or explain how to use a product. For example, a bicycle shop might help someone choose a suitable light and fit it correctly. That advice can be valuable even if the item is available elsewhere.', 'Ví dụ lợi ích dịch vụ cụ thể.'),
        p('Sinh hoạt khu phố','Finally, local shops help keep a neighbourhood active. Residents have places to meet briefly, exchange news and carry out small daily tasks on foot. A street with useful shops may feel more connected than one where people only leave by car to buy everything elsewhere. Accessibility and fair prices still matter if these shops are to serve different residents.', 'Không khẳng định mua tại địa phương luôn rẻ.'),
        p('Kết','In conclusion, local shops can support employment, provide individual help and strengthen everyday neighbourhood life. Buying locally when the products and prices suit our needs is one way to help those contributions continue.', 'Lời kết có cân nhắc khả năng chi trả.')],
    [q('Why do some people prefer large supermarkets?', 'They may find a wider range of products in one place and prefer predictable opening hours. For someone with little shopping time, that convenience can be important. Price comparisons also influence the choice.'),
     q('How can small shops compete with online sellers?', 'They can focus on useful advice, repairs or services that customers value locally. Clear online information about stock and opening hours can also help. They do not necessarily need to offer the lowest price on every item.'),
     q('Should people be expected to buy everything locally?', 'No. People have different budgets and needs, and some products may not be available nearby. I would encourage considering local options rather than making it a rule that ignores affordability or access.')],
    [('local employment','việc làm tại địa phương'),('personal attention','sự quan tâm riêng đến khách'),('regular customers','khách quen')]),
]
